Hi Jenna - Recently encountered the same error - client reported trouble getting an AICC package working - couple things turned up: Actual vs. expected .crs content: When the AICC .crs file is parsed in mod/scorm/datamodels/aicclib.php, line 164 expects a carriage return followed by newline: $rows = explode("
", $contents); The .crs raw output ( from Storyline) only included a newline ( 
 ) at the end of each line Thought about updating the .crs raw output but instead tested code to allow either delimiting pattern: $rows = preg_split("/(
|
)/", $contents); Also made this update to other similar code in the same function for parsing the other files in the AICC package The package loaded normally with no new errors in logs - tried your package as well and no problems sortorder = 0 in mdl_scorm_scoes After upload of the AICC package, launched the course and nothing displayed. Looked at the rows in mdl_scorm_scoes and noticed the sortorder value for the row with the launch file was 0.  This is normally something like 2 for many SCORM files. Switched this value to 2 and the package displayed Looked at the aicclib.php code for how sortorder is set, but nothing obvious and out of time to look for other causes Any chance you  Storyline for authoring?  Noticed Moodle has not updated the aicclib.php code in a while, so perhaps root cause is a recent change in how the files are exported from Storyline. Details on environment: Moodle 3.4.3 Linux Ubuntu 18.04 Apache 2.4.29 PHP 7.2.24 MySQL 5.7.28 Authoring tool used by client: Storyline Hope this is helpful!

