Hi All, in Moodle 1.9 filters act just before streaming the SCORM content to the browser, file.php : 
```text
    send_file($pathname, $filename, $lifetime, 
$CFG->filteruploadedfiles
, false, $forcedownload);
```
 In Moodle 2.x pluginfile.php delegates the streaming responsibility to each module. For SCORM it delegates to mod/scorm/lib.php::scorm_pluginfile() , that misses the 1.9 feature as well as any other module misses it. It seems a 2.x feature before being a missing/bug i.e. Moodle has been coded to perform that filtering no more. To activate the past behaviour, backup your mod/scorm/lib.php file and move the lines below from: 
```text
    // finally send the file


    send_stored_file($file, $lifetime, 
0
, false);


}
```
 to: 
```text
    // finally send the file


    send_stored_file($file, $lifetime, 
$CFG->filteruploadedfiles
, false);


}
```
 It should work even if the fix seems too easy, isn't it? Maybe some core developers will tell us the reason why filtering has been removed from these areas: mostly some known issues in 1.9 have promoted the idea to remove it in 2.x. I'll file this enh into the Tracker in case no one will reply in a week. HTH , Matteo

